/**
\fn void GameplayFramework::ActivateMouseStateSystem()
\ingroup gameplay
\brief Adds Components::FMouseState to ECS::GetGlobalSystemsEntity() and starts a system that tracks the mouse and the entity under it. Call once.

Defined at \src{src/Gameplay/Module.cpp,72,78}; the system itself is \src{src/Gameplay/Module.cpp,29,70}.
*/

/**
\struct Components::FColliderComponent
\ingroup gameplay
\brief One collision rectangle, `glm::vec4 ColliderShape`, relative to the entity's position. The engine does not interpret it; your systems do.

Defined at \src{include/Gameplay/Module.hpp,29,31}.
*/

/**
\struct Components::FMouseState
\ingroup gameplay
\brief The mouse position in world units (`MousePosition`) and the last entity under the cursor (`HoveredEntityId`, 0 if none yet).

Lives on ECS::GetGlobalSystemsEntity() once GameplayFramework::ActivateMouseStateSystem() has run. Read it with `ECS::GetGlobalSystemsEntity().get<Components::FMouseState>()`. Defined at \src{include/Gameplay/Components.hpp,15,18}.
*/
